    (when (and (!= (.-MergeLocalsHTrace base/Debug) 0) (>= selCount 2))
      (set! (.-trace cs) (.-MergeLocalsHTrace base/Debug)))))



























^{:go/end 625} (go/method populateIndirectUseTable "populateIndirectUseTable creates and populates the \"indirectUE\" table\nwithin cs by doing some additional analysis of how the vars in\ncands are accessed in the function.\n\nIt is possible to have situations where a given ir.Name is\nnon-address-taken at the source level, but whose address is\nmaterialized in order to accommodate the needs of\narchitecture-dependent operations or one sort or another (examples\ninclude things like LoweredZero/DuffZero, etc). The issue here is\nthat the SymAddr op will show up as touching a variable of\ninterest, but the subsequent memory op will not. This is generally\nnot an issue for computing whether something is live across a call,\nbut it is problematic for collecting the more fine-grained live\ninterval info that drives stack slot merging.\n\nTo handle this problem, make a forward pass over each basic block\nlooking for instructions of the form vK := SymAddr(N) where N is a\nraw candidate. Create an entry in a map at that point from vK to\nits use count. Continue the walk, looking for uses of vK: when we\nsee one, record it in a side table as an upwards exposed use of N.\nEach time we see a use, decrement the use count in the map, and if\nwe hit zero, remove the map entry. If we hit the end of the basic\nblock and we still have map entries, then evict the name in\nquestion from the candidate set.\n" [^{:tag (* cstate)} cs ^{:tag (slice (* ir/Name))} cands] :results [(slice (* ir/Name)) (slice candRegion)]

  ;; main indirect UE table, this is what we're producing in this func
